    "layout": [
      {
        "label": "prop:operations-algebra",
        "reason": "Keep short proposition statement together after actual build1 page review",
        "old": "\\begin{proposition}\\label{prop:operations-algebra}\nAddition and maximum are commutative and associative.  Translation\nsatisfies\n\\[\n \\begin{split}\n (\\Gamma+\\Gamma')+C\n   &=(\\Gamma+C)+\\Gamma'=\\Gamma+(\\Gamma'+C),\\\\\n (\\Gamma+C)+C'&=\\Gamma+(C+C'),\\\\\n (\\Gamma\\vee\\Gamma')+C\n   &=(\\Gamma+C)\\vee(\\Gamma'+C).\n \\end{split}\n\\tag{54.6}\\label{eq:operations-algebra}\n\\]\nAll identities are equalities of inverse systems, not merely equality\nup to $P$-equivalence.\n\\end{proposition}",
        "new": "\\par\\noindent\\begin{minipage}{\\textwidth}\n\\begin{proposition}\\label{prop:operations-algebra}\nAddition and maximum are commutative and associative.  Translation\nsatisfies\n\\[\n \\begin{split}\n (\\Gamma+\\Gamma')+C\n   &=(\\Gamma+C)+\\Gamma'=\\Gamma+(\\Gamma'+C),\\\\\n (\\Gamma+C)+C'&=\\Gamma+(C+C'),\\\\\n (\\Gamma\\vee\\Gamma')+C\n   &=(\\Gamma+C)\\vee(\\Gamma'+C).\n \\end{split}\n\\tag{54.6}\\label{eq:operations-algebra}\n\\]\nAll identities are equalities of inverse systems, not merely equality\nup to $P$-equivalence.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\end{minipage}\\par\\medskip"
      },
      {
        "label": "prop:operations-na-trace",
        "reason": "Keep short proposition statement together after actual build1 page review",
        "old": "\\begin{proposition}\\label{prop:operations-na-trace}\nFormula \\eqref{eq:operations-na-trace}, with the closed endpoint\nconvention \\eqref{eq:rays-test-endpoint}, is independent of all choices\nand defines\n\\[\n \\Tr_Y\\Gamma\\in\n \\PSH^{\\NA}(\\widetilde Y,\\rho^*\\theta).\n\\tag{54.31}\\label{eq:operations-na-trace-target}\n\\]\nFor $m=\\dim Y>0$, every target perturbation satisfies the uniform bound\n\\[\n \\int_{\\widetilde Y}\n \\bigl\\langle(\\beta_\\eta+\\ddc T_\\tau^\\eta)^m\\bigr\\rangle\n \\geq 2^{-m}\\int_{\\widetilde Y}\\eta^m>0\n \\quad(\\tau<c_Y(\\Gamma)).\n\\tag{54.31a}\\label{eq:operations-na-trace-mass-floor}\n\\]\nIf $\\pi:X'\\to X$ is proper bimeromorphic with $X'$ a smooth compact\nK\\\"ahler manifold, $Y$ is not contained in its non-isomorphism locus,\nand $Y'$ is the strict transform, then\n\\[\n \\widetilde\\pi^*\\Tr_Y\\Gamma\n =\\Tr_{Y'}(\\pi^*\\Gamma)\n\\tag{54.32}\\label{eq:operations-na-trace-birational}\n\\]\non the normalizations.  Here $\\widetilde\\pi$ is the induced proper\nbimeromorphic morphism of normal compact K\\\"ahler spaces; its metric\npullback uses \\cite[Section~4.8]{XiaOperationsV3}, which applies to\nthese possibly singular unibranch spaces.\n\\end{proposition}",
        "new": "\\par\\noindent\\begin{minipage}{\\textwidth}\n\\begin{proposition}\\label{prop:operations-na-trace}\nFormula \\eqref{eq:operations-na-trace}, with the closed endpoint\nconvention \\eqref{eq:rays-test-endpoint}, is independent of all choices\nand defines\n\\[\n \\Tr_Y\\Gamma\\in\n \\PSH^{\\NA}(\\widetilde Y,\\rho^*\\theta).\n\\tag{54.31}\\label{eq:operations-na-trace-target}\n\\]\nFor $m=\\dim Y>0$, every target perturbation satisfies the uniform bound\n\\[\n \\int_{\\widetilde Y}\n \\bigl\\langle(\\beta_\\eta+\\ddc T_\\tau^\\eta)^m\\bigr\\rangle\n \\geq 2^{-m}\\int_{\\widetilde Y}\\eta^m>0\n \\quad(\\tau<c_Y(\\Gamma)).\n\\tag{54.31a}\\label{eq:operations-na-trace-mass-floor}\n\\]\nIf $\\pi:X'\\to X$ is proper bimeromorphic with $X'$ a smooth compact\nK\\\"ahler manifold, $Y$ is not contained in its non-isomorphism locus,\nand $Y'$ is the strict transform, then\n\\[\n \\widetilde\\pi^*\\Tr_Y\\Gamma\n =\\Tr_{Y'}(\\pi^*\\Gamma)\n\\tag{54.32}\\label{eq:operations-na-trace-birational}\n\\]\non the normalizations.  Here $\\widetilde\\pi$ is the induced proper\nbimeromorphic morphism of normal compact K\\\"ahler spaces; its metric\npullback uses \\cite[Section~4.8]{XiaOperationsV3}, which applies to\nthese possibly singular unibranch spaces.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\end{minipage}\\par\\medskip"
